.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":null,"_gp_sbc_dilution":null,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.00849,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":5.7,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"SELLAS Life Sciences Group, Inc., a late-stage clinical biopharmaceutical company, focuses on the development of novel therapeutics for various cancer indications in the United States. The company's lead product candidate is galinpepimut-S (GPS), a peptide immunotherapy directed against the Wilms tumor 1, antigen; and SLS009 (tambiciclib), a selective small molecule cyclin-dependent kinase 9, or CDK9, inhibitor. It has a strategic collaboration with Merck & Co., Inc. to evaluate GPS as it is administered in combination with PD1 blocker pembrolizumab in a Phase 1/2 clinical trial enrolling patients in up to five cancer indications, including hematologic malignancies and solid tumors; GenFleet Therapeutics (Shanghai), Inc. for the development and commercialization of GFH009; and Memorial Sloan Kettering Cancer Center for developing and commercializing MSK's WT1 peptide vaccine technology. SELLAS Life Sciences Group, Inc. is headquartered in New York, New York.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Angelos M. Stergiou M.D., ScD h.c. | Founder, President, CEO & Director | Age 49 | Compensation: $1.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 13 people. Stock-based compensation of $150K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["SELLAS Life Sciences Group, Inc is a mid-cap healthcare business with a $3.0B market cap.","The top line has compounded at -52% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at -239% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 2/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (28.1% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Healthcare peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Healthcare peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (25.6% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"(SLS) Movement Within Algorithmic Entry Frameworks","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.c